{
  "heading": "Outgoing HTTP: Tac",
  "axis": "language",
  "summary": "In the browser, HTTPClient is the auto-managed transport. HTTPClient takes only cache: no-store by default, or cache-first, network-first or reload. A Tac HTTPClient must declare at least one request method, such as GetRequest. This transport works only in the browser (ADR 0027). A @standalone HTTPClient role marker in a native Tac companion fails with TY1308. So Swift, Kotlin, C#, Rust and Go keep HTTP request annotations on a service that owns its context and names an explicitly configured HTTP adapter. Dart does the same: the auto-managed transport is not available to a Dart service either, and a standalone HTTPClient role marker there also fails with TY1308. A request to another origin needs its host in `tac.outgoing.hosts`: the build checks request URLs, and the page's `connect-src` lets the browser reach only these hosts.",
